# Grosyhub Shopify theme deployment

## Critical: dev vs live are different themes

| What | Theme | ID | URL |
|------|-------|-----|-----|
| **LIVE** (what customers see) | `grosyhub/main` | `#185016090669` | `grasyhub.com` |
| **Dev/preview** (`theme dev`) | `Development (2d9412-...)` | `#186228867117` | `127.0.0.1:9292` or preview link |

`shopify theme dev` syncs only to the **development** theme. Changes there do **not** appear on `grasyhub.com`.

## When the user wants changes on the live store

Always push to the live theme explicitly:

```bash
shopify theme push --live --theme 185016090669 --allow-live --store igh9a1-1h.myshopify.com
```

For specific files:

```bash
shopify theme push --live --theme 185016090669 --allow-live --store igh9a1-1h.myshopify.com --only "path/to/file.liquid,path/to/file.css"
```

Never assume `theme dev` or a push without `--live` updates the production site.

## After every live push — verify

Pull the same file from live and confirm it changed:

```bash
shopify theme pull --live --theme 185016090669 --store igh9a1-1h.myshopify.com --only "snippets/changed-file.liquid" --path ".live-check"
```

Compare pulled content to local before telling the user the live site is updated.

## Tell the user clearly

- **Preview/dev**: `http://127.0.0.1:9292` or the `preview_theme_id` URL from `theme dev`
- **Live site**: `https://grasyhub.com` — only updates after `theme push --live`
